# A plain segment for the real Pi (docs/user_guide/pi_setup.md). Copy to
# /etc/pi-fortress/segments.d/<name>.env and run `pf apply`. The file
# name is the segment name. To remove the segment, delete the file and
# apply again. This file is the desktop seat, which shares the agent cable
# as 802.1Q VLAN 79.
#
# A plain segment is treated as a machine that may be compromised. It
# resolves through the Pi with the agent block lists. It connects only to
# addresses that its DNS gave (any port). It cannot reach local addresses.
# It gets no QUIC, DoT or DoH. It uses the strict ports of the house, so SSH
# goes out only to the ssh_allow.ips of the agent. Without INSPECT=on
# (below), it gets no HTTPS inspection, no site-name check and no
# credential substitution.
#
# The interface. A dot makes it an 802.1Q child, parent.vlan-id. apply
# then creates the VLAN profile, and also a profile with no address for
# the parent trunk port. A VLAN on the HOUSE_IF cable (one per SSID of
# the house AP) has house trust at most: apply refuses ADMIN=yes and
# SSH_TO there, and warns that it is only as isolated as the AP.
IF=eth0.79
NET=10.79.0.0/30
IP=10.79.0.1
# yes lets this segment ssh to the Pi itself. `make pi-ship` runs from
# the desk seat, so the desk seat needs this. A guest segment does not.
ADMIN=yes
# One address or an a-b range inside AGENT_NET that this segment may
# reach on tcp 22, and nothing else. This is the operator path to the
# agent VMs after their VirtualBox NAT adapter is cut. Empty for no hole.
SSH_TO=10.77.0.10-10.77.0.12
# The gate: new connections, any port, only to addresses that the
# resolver of this segment gave.
# "off" removes it, for a host that runs software that dials addresses that
# it got out of band. The Tailscale relays are the known case.
#BLOCK_DIRECT_IP=on
# Ports: strict (web, mail and push, time, ping, and SSH to
# ssh_allow.ips only), audit (log what strict would drop, pass it) or
# open. ALLOW_PORTS adds to strict.
#EGRESS=strict
#ALLOW_PORTS="tcp:5000-5002 udp:3478"
# One address that may ssh INTO this segment (an admin laptop on the house
# network), never from the uplink. The segment never gets a path back to it.
# Never an agent address: apply refuses one inside AGENT_NET.
#SSH_FROM=10.78.0.20
# DNS here answers only addresses and refuses key-shaped names, as for the
# agent. Record types that the software of this desk still needs (Teams, XMPP
# and mail autodiscover use SRV; some SSO and VPN clients use TXT):
#DNS_TYPES="SRV TXT"
# on: the Pi leases addresses on this segment from DHCP_START to
# DHCP_END (inside NET, never IP or the network or broadcast address of NET),
# with IP as router and DNS, and a 12h lease. It has its own DHCP-only
# dnsmasq, pi-fortress-dhcp@<segment>. For devices that cannot use a static
# address, for example IoT on a VLAN per SSID of the house AP. It is allowed
# there, and the AP must not run its own DHCP on that SSID (in AP mode it does
# not). off, the default, keeps the segment static. If you set it to off or
# delete the file, the instance stops, and its conf and leases are removed.
# This /30 has one address to lease, in addition to IP.
#DHCP=off
#DHCP_START=10.79.0.2
#DHCP_END=10.79.0.2
# on: the fence of the agent network for this desk too. All HTTPS (tcp 443)
# of the segment goes through the engine and the broker. The tools of the
# desk hold placeholders, the Pi puts in the real key only for the service
# that owns it, and live keys in known formats are stripped. The desk must
# trust the CA of the Pi first, or no HTTPS works:
#   on the desk: ssh -t <user>@<pi> 'sudo install -m 0644 /var/lib/pi-fortress/engine/ca-cert.pem /tmp/pf-ca.pem && sha256sum /tmp/pf-ca.pem'
#                scp <user>@<pi>:/tmp/pf-ca.pem ~/pf-ca.pem
#                sudo vm/desk/setup.sh ca ~/pf-ca.pem <sha256>
# (docs/user_guide/pi_setup.md, "The credential fence on the desk").
# Software that pins its own certificates (some banking, VPN and update
# clients) fails through the fence. Turn it off with INSPECT=off and pf
# apply. With ADMIN=yes on the same segment, apply warns: the SSH key for
# the Pi on this desk opens all real keys, so protect that key. Not allowed
# on the house cable. Needs BLOCK_DIRECT_IP on.
#INSPECT=off
# on: this segment resolves only the names in
# /etc/pi-fortress/allow.<segment>.domains (apply seeds it with the
# Anthropic names the first time; docs/paranoid_mode.md). It does not
# depend on PARANOID in net.env. Needs BLOCK_DIRECT_IP on.
#PARANOID=off
# Connection budgets of this segment only (internal/render/connlimit.go).
# Each key that is not set takes the SEG_ value from net.env. 0 disables
# one. Live flows per device, new flows a second per device as RATE/BURST,
# live flows for the whole segment, and new TCP flows a second for the whole
# segment as RATE/BURST. The defaults are the agent segment values. A desktop
# browser with hundreds of open tabs can go above 128 live flows, and
# CONN_PER_IP=512 is the setting for it.
#CONN_PER_IP=128
#NEW_PER_IP=50/200
#CONN_TOTAL=4096
#NEW_TOTAL=300/600
